Hi <%= @user.login %>,

Some IP addresses on your account are not assigned to a VPS. We plan to
release them so other users can use them.
<% if @addresses.any?(&:public_ipv4?) -%>

Public IPv4 addresses are a scarce resource. Releasing addresses you no longer
need helps make room for other VPSes.
<% end -%>

<% @addresses.each do |item| -%>
  - <%= item.address %>/<%= item.prefix %> (<%= item.location_label || 'location unavailable' %>)
<% end -%>

Planned release date: <%= local_time(@campaign.deadline, '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M %Z') %>

If you no longer need these addresses, you do not need to reply or do
anything.

If you still need an address, you can keep it by assigning it to a VPS.
<% if @campaign.allow_keep -%>
You can also keep an address unassigned: select it in vpsAdmin and enter a
reason why you need it.
<% else -%>
Keeping an unassigned address requires an administrator's exemption.
Previously submitted reasons do not prevent release under the current policy.
<% end -%>

You can see the current address status and options for keeping them in
vpsAdmin:
<%= @webui_url %>/?page=ip_release&action=request&id=<%= @request.id %>

Thank you for helping make unused addresses available to other users.

Best regards,
vpsAdmin
